--- a/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/699-netfilter-flowtable-set-out-ifindex-when-the-forward.patch
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,59 +0,0 @@
-From: Hauke Mehrtens <hauke@hauke-m.de>
-Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 22:15:00 +0200
-Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: set out ifindex when the forward path
- is unknown
-
-Since commit b5964aac51e0 ("netfilter: flowtable: consolidate xmit path")
-the FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH path does not transmit on the dst device any
-more, it looks the output device up by the interface index stored in the
-flow tuple:
-
-	xmit.outdev = dev_get_by_index_rcu(state->net, tuplehash->tuple.ifidx);
-	if (!xmit.outdev) {
-		flow_offload_teardown(flow);
-		return NF_DROP;
-	}
-
-That index comes from route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex, which is only
-assigned in nft_dev_forward_path() when the forward path could be
-discovered.  nft_default_forward_path() never sets it, so a flow whose
-egress path cannot be resolved is offloaded with an interface index of 0.
-Every packet of such a flow is then dropped while the flow entry is torn
-down, and the flow_offload expression offloads it again right away, so
-the loss repeats instead of settling.
-
-This is easy to hit on a router that bridges Wi-Fi and Ethernet:
-mac80211 returns -EOPNOTSUPP from .ndo_fill_forward_path when the driver
-does not implement .net_fill_forward_path, and dev_fill_forward_path()
-turns any error into a failure of the whole path lookup.  Traffic towards
-Wi-Fi clients then loses a packet per re-offload cycle, which shows up as
-sporadic stalls and lost UDP datagrams rather than as a hard failure.
-
-Fall back to the dst device, which is the device the neighbour is looked
-up on and the device the packet was transmitted on before the two xmit
-paths were merged.
-
-Mainline avoids the situation differently since commit 871df5007eda
-("netfilter: flowtable: bail out if forward path cannot be discovered"),
-which refuses to offload the flow at all.  That change sits on top of the
-forward path discovery rework and does not apply to 6.18.y, and it also
-gives up the offload for flows that were offloaded successfully before,
-so restoring the previous behaviour is the minimal fix here.
-
-Fixes: b5964aac51e0 ("netfilter: flowtable: consolidate xmit path")
-Signed-off-by: Hauke Mehrtens <hauke@hauke-m.de>
